uploads/

# loadtest-results/ deliberately stays tracked: the CI report publisher commits
# there by design, and `git add loadtest-results` (no -f) only works while the
# directory is not ignored.
#
# A warning here used to say the committed reports contain request bodies and a
# 6-character API key prefix. They do not: loadtest-results/lab/api-restart.log
# carries 5,156 `[redacted]` markers and no `"body"` entries, and a sweep of the
# directory finds no DATABASE_URL, REDIS_URL, DASHBOARD_SECRET, ADMIN_SECRET,
# bearer token or unredacted key. The only phone-shaped values are synthetic
# load-test fixtures (251900000000 and generated sequences).
#
# Keep it that way: if the report publisher ever starts committing a raw server
# log again, that is a credential leak into git history, and history has to be
# rewritten to undo it. Re-run that sweep before committing new results.

# Stale patch files. cbe-receipt-fix.patch was committed at the root and applied
# to nothing — `git apply --check` failed forwards and backwards against every
# file it named. A patch in the tree that does not apply reads as "a fix that was
# meant to be here" and wastes whoever picks it up next.
*.patch
*.orig
*.rej
